to surpass, overcome;
to escape;
 neglect;
to pass away, die.

अति-√ चर् to pass by;
to overtake, surpass;
to transgress, offend, be unfaithful to.

अति-√ तप् to be very hot, AV. xviii, 2, 36, &c.;
to heat, AV. xiii, 2, 40; BhP.;
to affect greatly:
Caus. -तापयति, to heat much.

अति-√ नी to lead over or beyond, to help a person over anything, RV. &c.;
to allow to pass away:
Intens. Ā. -नेनीय॑ते, to bring forward, RV. vi, 47, 16.

अति-√ पद् to go beyond (acc.), jump over;
to neglect, transgress:
Caus. -पादयति to allow to pass by.

अति-√ 1. पृ to convey across, to help over, RV.;
to cross, pass over, RV. i, 174, 9 and vi, 20, 12;
to keep (a promise) :
Caus. -पारयति to lead or convey over, RV. &c.

अति-√ भू (perf. -बभूव), to originate or take rise in an excessive way, MBh. viii, 4541;
 P. (once Ā. TĀr.), to excel, surpass, PBr.; MBh. &c.:
Desid. to intend to surpass, ĀśvŚr.

अति-√ मन् -मन्यते (1. pl. -मनामहे॑ऽति), to disdain, despise, RV. &c.;
to value less than one's self, ŚBr.;
to pride one's self, ŚBr.

अति-√ या to pass over or before;
to surpass, RV. &c.;
to pass by, RV. i, 135, 7;
to transgress, BhP.

अति-√ रिच् Pass. -रिच्यते, to be left with a surplus, to surpass (in a good or bad sense with abl. or acc.);
to be superior, predominate, prevail:
Caus. -रेचयति, to do superfluously, to do too much, ŚBr. &c.

अति-रेक or अती-रेक॑ [only once, ŚBr.], अस्, m. surplus, excess
 redundancy;
 difference.

